menu "P1 Dongle Configuration"

    config P1_UART_NUM
        int "UART peripheral number for the P1 port"
        default 1
        range 0 2
        help
            Hardware UART used to read the P1 telegram. UART0 is normally the
            console, so use UART1 (default) on the Universal P1 Dongle.

    config P1_UART_RX_GPIO
        int "P1 UART RX GPIO"
        default 1
        help
            GPIO connected to the P1 data line (via the on-board inverting
            transistor). On the Leotro Universal P1 Dongle this is GPIO1.

    config P1_REQUEST_GPIO
        int "P1 data-request GPIO"
        default 2
        help
            GPIO that drives the smart meter's data-request line (through the
            opto-isolator). On the Leotro Universal P1 Dongle this is GPIO2.

    config P1_UART_BAUD_RATE
        int "P1 UART baud rate"
        default 115200
        help
            115200 for DSMR 4.x/5.x meters (NL/BE), 9600 for older DSMR 2.2/3.

    config P1_REQUEST_ACTIVE
        bool "Hold the data-request line active"
        default y
        help
            When enabled the request line is driven high so a DSMR 4/5 meter
            streams a telegram roughly every second.

    config P1_INVERT_RX
        bool "Invert the P1 RX signal in software"
        default n
        help
            Enable when the P1 data line reaches the RX GPIO WITHOUT an on-board
            inverting transistor/opto (i.e. the raw, inverted open-collector P1
            signal is wired more or less directly, as on a repurposed board). The
            Leotro dongle inverts in hardware, so leave this OFF for it. Symptom of
            needing it: raw RX shows garbage bytes instead of '/'-prefixed ASCII.

    config P1_VERIFY_CRC
        bool "Verify telegram CRC16"
        default y
        help
            Validate the CRC16 that DSMR 4/5 meters append to each telegram and
            drop corrupted frames. Disable for DSMR 2.2/3 meters without a CRC.

    config P1_PASSTHROUGH
        bool "Enable P1 passthrough to the second port"
        default y
        help
            Relay each telegram received from the meter out of the dongle's
            second P1 port (P1TX), so a downstream device (e.g. a HomeWizard P1
            meter) connected there reads the same data. Matter monitoring and
            passthrough run from the same meter read.

    config P1_TX_GPIO
        int "Passthrough TX GPIO (data out to downstream device)"
        default 42
        depends on P1_PASSTHROUGH
        help
            GPIO driving the second P1 port's data line (via the on-board
            transistor). On the Leotro Universal P1 Dongle this is GPIO42.

    config P1_PASSTHROUGH_HONOR_REQUEST
        bool "Only relay while the downstream device requests data"
        default n
        depends on P1_PASSTHROUGH
        help
            When enabled, telegrams are forwarded only while the downstream
            device asserts its data-request line. Leave disabled to stream
            continuously (works with HomeWizard and most readers).

    config P1_TXREQ_GPIO
        int "Downstream data-request input GPIO (TXREQ)"
        default 41
        depends on P1_PASSTHROUGH_HONOR_REQUEST
        help
            GPIO that senses the downstream device's data-request line. On the
            Leotro Universal P1 Dongle this is GPIO41.

endmenu

menu "Example Configuration"

    config ENABLE_MEMORY_PROFILING
        bool "Enable Memory Profiling"
        default n
        help
            Enable this option to include memory profiling features in the example.
            This will allow you to monitor memory usage during runtime.

endmenu
